\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. How can a sinner know
\par His sins on earth forgiven?
\par How can my gracious Saviour show
\par My name inscribed in heaven?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. What we have felt and seen
\par With  confidence we tell;
\par And publish to the sons of men
\par The signs infallible.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. We who in Christ believe
\par That He for us hath died,
\par We all His unknown peace receive
\par And feel His blood applied.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Exults our rising soul,
\par Disburdened of her load,
\par And swells unutterably full
\par Of glory and of God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. His love, surpassing far
\par The love of all beneath,
\par We find within our hearts, and dare
\par The pointless darts of death.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Stronger than death and hell
\par The mystic power we prove;
\par And conquerors of the world, we dwell
\par In heaven, who dwell  in love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. His Spirit to us He gave,
\par And dwells in us we know;
\par The witness in ourselves we have,
\par And all its fruits we show.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Whate'er our pardoning Lord
\par Commands, we gladly do;
\par And guided by His sacred word,
\par We all His steps pursue.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

